  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>eflornithine</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>D11AX16</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, oral dosing <small>(PK_1C_enteral)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Jansson R et al. 2008</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>male Sprague-Dawley rats</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>eflornithine</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_eflornithine/Eflornithine_Jansson2008_value_for_l_eflornithine\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>T max (mol/min/kg of body wt)</td><td>14.5</td><td>h</td><td><small>tmax</small></td></tr><tr><td>F (%) at 750 to 2,000 mg/kg of body wt</td><td>62.3</td><td></td><td><small>Fab</small></td></tr><tr><td>CL (ml/min/kg of body wt)</td><td>14.5</td><td>ml/min/kg</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>V central (liters/kg of body wt)</td><td>0.404</td><td>L/kg</td><td><small>V</small></td></tr><tr><td>K a (h -1 )</td><td>1.16</td><td>h -1</td><td><small>kabs</small></td></tr><tr><td>T lag (h)</td><td>0.447</td><td>h</td><td><small>tlag</small></td></tr></table><h4>About eflornithine</h4><p>Eflornithine is used to treat excessive facial hair growth in women (hirsutism) and, in combination therapy, the childhood cancer neuroblastoma; it has also been used against sleeping sickness. It remains authorised in the European Union for these uses, with a topical dermatological product for hirsutism and an oncology product for neuroblastoma, though some applications have been withdrawn.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q72470623\">Wikidata Q72470623</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Eflornithine\">Eflornithine</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Jansson R et al. (2008). Enantioselective and nonlinear intestinal absorption of eflornithine in the rat. <i>Antimicrobial agents and chemotherapy 52(8):2842–2848</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1128/AAC.00050-08\">10.1128/AAC.00050-08</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18519728\">18519728</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Jansson_2008: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"),
    experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 86400, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Eflornithine_Jansson2008_value_for_l_eflornithine;
